# No em dash (`—`) for empty UI

Do **not** show `—` (or `--`) when a list cell, table field, tag column, or stat has no value. Leave the cell **blank**.

- Tables: `{{ value }}` or conditional blocks — not `?? '—'` / `|| '—'`.
- Tag chips: `@empty` shows nothing (see `app-tag-chip-list`).
- Task Manager empty custom fields: empty `.tm-cell-placeholder` (no character).
- Select placeholders: use helpful text (e.g. “Select project”) or omit `placeholder`, not `—`.
- Prose, titles, and labels may still use an em dash in running copy (e.g. “Bookings — Type name”).
